/-!
# The graded layers of a twist have no higher cohomology, over a Noetherian local base

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring, let `f : X ⟶ Spec A` be proper, let `ℒ` be an invertible
`𝒪_X`-module and `ℱ` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type, and write
`ℱ(d) = ℱ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℒ ^⊗ d`.  Let `v : V ⟶ X` be the closed immersion cut out by `𝔪 𝒪_X` — the
fibre of `f` over the closed point — lying over `Spec(A ⧸ 𝔪)` by a proper `g`.  If `v ^* ℒ` is
ample on `V`, then there is a `d₀` with

`H ᵖ(X, 𝔪 ⁿ ℱ(d) / 𝔪 ⁿ⁺¹ ℱ(d)) = 0`  for every `d ≥ d₀`, every `p > 0` and every `n`,

one exponent serving every `n`.

This is the hypothesis `hgr` of assertion (B) of [Stacks, Tag 0D2M] over a local base,
`Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.exists_surjective_fibreCohomology_twistModule`, and it is
where ampleness on the fibre and the choice of `d₀` live.  With it that assertion stands at the
source's own hypotheses.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GradedProperCohomology.exists_isZero_rightDerived_kernelIdealPowerQuotientDropTwist`:
  the vanishing above.

## The route

The file instantiates part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0897] at the fibre and rewrites its conclusion
into the form used by the two assertions of [Stacks, Tag 0D2M].

* **The engine.** `exists_isZero_Hgroup_tensorPowTwist_int_fibreAssociatedGraded_of_isAffine`
  concludes the vanishing of `H ᵖ(V, (⨁ₙ v ^*(𝔪 ⁿ ℱ))ₙ ⊗ (v ^* ℒ) ^⊗ d)` on the fibre, in the
  group-valued model of cohomology.  Its base is `S = Spec A`, affine, which is what makes the
  chartwise surjectivity of [Stacks, Tag 01OG] available for the local surjectivity of `Θ` —
  `Spec A` serving as its own affine chart — and that is the only place affineness enters.
* **Its three remaining data.** Properness of `g` and ampleness on the fibre are hypotheses here,
  as they are in the source.  The Noetherian `k`-algebra with its identification of the global
  sections of `⨁ₙ j ^*(𝔪 ⁿ)` is `AssociatedGraded.gradedRing 𝔪`, Noetherian by
  `AssociatedGraded.isNoetherianRing_gradedRing`, with `ρ` and `hρ` given by
  `Stacks.Conormal.specGradedPullbackSectionsRingEquiv` and its `_algebraMap` companion, whose
  own hypothesis is discharged at the ideal sheaf used here by
  `Stacks.Conormal.ker_app_top_quotImmersion_eq_specIdealSheaf`.  Ampleness upstairs on the
  relative spectrum is [Stacks, Tag 0892] part (2) for an affine morphism,
  `Stacks.AmplePullback.isAmple_modulePullback_of_isAffineHom`, the structure morphism of a
  relative spectrum being affine.
* **The two rewritings.** The scheme and the cohomology functor are moved by
  `Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions.isZero_rightDerived_pushforward_iff_isZero_hgroup`, and the
  identification of the transition kernel of the adic tower of the twist with the direct image of
  the twisted layer on the fibre is
  `Stacks.Algebraization.kernelIdealPowerQuotientDropTwistReesIso`.  The ideal sheaf the engine
  works with is the inverse image of the one generated by `𝔪` on `Spec A`, which is `𝔪 𝒪_X` by
  `Stacks.PuncturedSpectrumPicard.baseIdealSheaf_eq_comap`.

## No attribute

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is one input of the two assertions of
[Stacks, Tag 0D2M] and not itself the assertion of a numbered result.  Part (2) of
[Stacks, Tag 0897] already carries its attributes where it is proved.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0897](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0897)
